    "id": "what",
    "eyebrow": "The structure",
    "heading": "An odd-runs zone and a periodic block",
    "html": "<p>The head sweeps from end to end; each round trip adds one cell at the left end and three at the right. The leftward sweep is simple: C runs left over the 1s, and each 0 it meets (with a 1 before it) moves one cell to the left (<code>1 1 C&gt;0</code> becomes <code>C&gt;1 0 1</code>). The rightward sweep zigzags over the left zone and then runs straight through the block to the right end.</p><p>The right part of the tape is the word <code>01011111</code> repeated, a steady 60% of it; the sweeps cross it word by word (proved). The left 40% is irregular, but every run of 1s in it has odd length and every 0 is single, at every sweep end ever looked at; so it is a list of odd numbers, and every round trip rewrites the list.</p><figure style=\"margin:1rem 0\"><img alt=\"The tape at every visit to the left end, the first 1.2·10&lt;sup&gt;6&lt;/sup&gt; steps, one row per visit (dark: 1). The regular stripes on the right are the periodic block; the left zone is the irregular texture.\" src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" style=\"width:100%;max-width:900px;height:auto;image-rendering:auto;border:1px solid var(--line)\"/><figcaption style=\"font-size:.9rem;color:var(--fg2)\">The tape at every visit to the left end, the first 1.2·10<sup>6</sup> steps, one row per visit (dark: 1). The regular stripes on the right are the periodic block; the left zone is the irregular texture.</figcaption></figure>"
