    "eyebrow": "Proved in Lean",
    "heading": "The sweep rules",
    "html": "<p>Each row is a theorem of <code>lean/Rules.lean</code>, for every <code>n</code> and every tape <code>L</code>, <code>R</code> (<code>S&gt;</code>: the head in state S on the next cell; <code>(w)^n</code>: n copies of w; <code>0^inf</code>: blank tape).</p><div style=\"overflow-x:auto\"><table class=\"tbl\"><thead><tr><th>rule</th><th>from</th><th>to</th><th>steps</th><th>what it says</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><code>left_ones</code></td><td><code>L 1^n C&gt; 1 R</code></td><td><code>L C&gt; 1 (1)^n R</code></td><td>n</td><td>Leftward sweep: C runs left over ones (C1 = 1LC).</td></tr><tr><td><code>shift_zero</code></td><td><code>L 1 1 C&gt; 0 R</code></td><td><code>L C&gt; 1 0 1 R</code></td><td>2</td><td>Leftward sweep at a 0 after a 1: C writes 1 and D writes 0 one cell further left, so the 0 moves one cell left.</td></tr><tr><td><code>left_block</code></td><td><code>L (11010111)^n C&gt; 1 R</code></td><td><code>L C&gt; 1 (01011111)^n R</code></td><td>8 · n</td><td>Leftward sweep over the periodic block on the right: each 11010111 becomes 01011111 (8 steps a word).</td></tr><tr><td><code>right_block</code></td><td><code>L B&gt; (11111010)^n R</code></td><td><code>L (10101111)^n B&gt; R</code></td><td>8 · n</td><td>Rightward sweep over the periodic block: B turns each 11111010 into 10101111 (8 steps a word).</td></tr><tr><td><code>right_E</code></td><td><code>L E&gt; (011)^n R</code></td><td><code>L (110)^n E&gt; R</code></td><td>3 · n</td><td>Rightward sweep: E turns 011 into 110.</td></tr><tr><td><code>right_A</code></td><td><code>L A&gt; (101)^n R</code></td><td><code>L (011)^n A&gt; R</code></td><td>3 · n</td><td>Rightward sweep: A turns 101 into 011.</td></tr><tr><td><code>right_F</code></td><td><code>L F&gt; (110)^n R</code></td><td><code>L (101)^n F&gt; R</code></td><td>3 · n</td><td>Rightward sweep: F turns 110 into 101.</td></tr><tr><td><code>right_end</code></td><td><code>L 0 1 0 1 1 F&gt; 1 0^inf</code></td><td><code>L C&gt; 0 0 1 1 1